means of course that
today's show will air,

267
00:13:39,786 --> 00:13:42,554
but you, my dear,
are out of a job.

268
00:13:42,622 --> 00:13:44,923
I don't believe this.

269
00:13:46,993 --> 00:13:49,627
Poor little Lisa's in shock.

270
00:13:49,696 --> 00:13:51,662
But tastefully.

271
00:13:51,731 --> 00:13:53,197
You're insane!

272
00:13:53,266 --> 00:13:54,932
This is all a game to you!

273
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:56,433
You don't even deserve to live!

274
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:57,680
Temper, temper.

275
00:13:57,704 --> 00:13:58,903
Oh, did I mention to you

276
00:13:58,972 --> 00:14:01,216
that I need your offices cleaned
out by tomorrow morning?

277
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,252
There's some empty
boxes in the mailroom.

278
00:14:03,276 --> 00:14:05,209
Say, why don't you ask?

279
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:23,360
Lisa?

280
00:14:23,429 --> 00:14:25,362
Lisa?

281
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:54,491
Still here?

282
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:55,826
Why not?

283
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,828
You have nowhere to go.

284
00:15:41,808 --> 00:15:43,774
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

285
00:15:43,843 --> 00:15:45,821
You came all this
way for nothing.

286
00:15:45,845 --> 00:15:47,611
No, the trip was fine.

287
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,525
But I want nothing
to do with this show...

288
00:15:49,549 --> 00:15:51,982
This<i> Real Law...</i> if Dan
Galloway is gonna do it.

289
00:15:52,051 --> 00:15:54,029
I don't think
Dan'll do the show.

290
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:55,631
It's not exactly his style.

291
00:15:55,655 --> 00:15:57,254
Style.

292
00:15:57,323 --> 00:15:59,283
When did being a
jerk become a style?

293
00:15:59,325 --> 00:16:00,458
Hmm.

294
00:16:00,526 --> 00:16:02,137
Well, at least we've
had some time together.

295
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:03,972
Yeah. Lisa Bateman? Yes?

296
00:16:03,996 --> 00:16:05,929
I'm Lieutenant Burner
of the Los Angeles Police.

297
00:16:05,998 --> 00:16:07,464
We have a warrant
for your arrest.

298
00:16:07,533 --> 00:16:08,899
What?

299
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:11,268
You're being charged with
the murder of Dan Galloway.

300
00:16:11,338 --> 00:16:13,170
You have the right
to remain silent.

301
00:16:13,239 --> 00:16:14,884
If you give up that right,

302
00:16:14,908 --> 00:16:16,852
anything you say or do can
and will be used against you

303
00:16:16,876 --> 00:16:18,709
in a court of law.

304
00:16:27,354 --> 00:16:29,286
Don't say another word, Lisa.

305
00:16:29,356 --> 00:16:31,288
Ben and I are
going to defend you.

306
00:16:31,358 --> 00:16:33,458
I can't tell you how
much I appreciate this.

307
00:16:33,526 --> 00:16:34,892
What are friends for?

308
00:16:34,961 --> 00:16:38,896
Well, they got a pretty
good case against you.

309
00:16:38,965 --> 00:16:42,199
You were in the building
at the time of the murder,

310
00:16:42,268 --> 00:16:45,202
an eyewitness heard
you threaten him,

311
00:16:45,271 --> 00:16:47,605
and your fingerprints are
all over the murder weapon.

312
00:16:47,674 --> 00:16:50,875
Ben, the only time I saw
that axe was in his office.

313
00:16:50,943 --> 00:16:52,376
And I left it there.

314
00:16:52,445 --> 00:16:55,446
Well, who else could've
gotten hold of it?

315
00:16:55,515 --> 00:16:57,448
Anyone.

316
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,249
Anyone who works in the studio.

317
00:16:59,319 --> 00:17:01,352
Anyone who had a
pass to the building today.

318
00:17:01,421 --> 00:17:04,087
The three women who were
on the show this afternoon...

319
00:17:04,156 --> 00:17:06,791
They were all angry
enough to want to kill him.

320
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,893
Hmm.

321
00:17:08,962 --> 00:17:11,863
Well, how can we see
a tape of that show?

322
00:17:22,942 --> 00:17:25,143
You find anything? Not much...

323
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:27,578
Matches, the top of
a pen, all the typical

324
00:17:27,647 --> 00:17:29,647
of what you'd find on
the floor of an office.

325
00:17:33,019 --> 00:17:35,886
They tracing this?

326
00:17:35,955 --> 00:17:37,566
According to the police,
that button wasn't found

327
00:17:37,590 --> 00:17:40,190
on any of the clothing Joe was
wearing the day of the murder.

328
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,238
Not that that helps; it could
have dropped off anytime.

329
00:17:42,262 --> 00:17:43,193
Well, yeah,

330
00:17:43,263 --> 00:17:45,496
yeah, yeah, but...

331
00:17:45,565 --> 00:17:48,366
doesn't a cleaning crew
come in here every night?

332
00:17:48,434 --> 00:17:50,646
Sure, they do, but with the
way people clean nowadays,

333
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:52,782
we figure it could have
been here for months.

334
00:17:52,806 --> 00:17:54,316
Yeah.

335
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,819
You mind if I hang on to this?

336
00:17:56,843 --> 00:17:57,920
Well, with your
client's fingerprints

337
00:17:57,944 --> 00:17:59,276
all over the murder weapon...

338
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:01,323
Yeah, you probably
won't be needing this.

339
00:18:01,347 --> 00:18:03,380
I won't let it get away from me.

340
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:09,464
Was this machine unplugged
when the body was found?

341
00:18:09,488 --> 00:18:10,633
Must have been.

342
00:18:10,657 --> 00:18:12,857
We searched the room;
nobody changed anything.

343
00:18:12,926 --> 00:18:15,192
Hmm. Huh.

344
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:17,561
Hmm.

345
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:18,774
I'll be right back.

346
00:18:18,798 --> 00:18:20,731
Yeah.

347
00:18:28,541 --> 00:18:29,840
Excuse me.

348
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:30,841
Can I help you?

349
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:32,343
I sure hope so.

350
00:18:32,412 --> 00:18:34,678
I'm investigating
Mr. Galloway's murder.

351
00:18:34,747 --> 00:18:36,747
I was home when it happened.

352
00:18:36,816 --> 00:18:39,183
No, no, I'm not
investigating you.

353
00:18:39,251 --> 00:18:41,096
When you finish using
one of these machines,

354
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,419
do you unplug it?

355
00:18:42,489 --> 00:18:43,554
Unplug it?

356
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:45,322
No, it's like a TV set.

357
00:18:45,391 --> 00:18:47,303
You just turn it off
when you're through.

358
00:18:47,327 --> 00:18:50,227
Huh, so if one of these
machines is unplugged,

359
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:53,230
would you say someone
unplugged it on purpose?

360
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:55,099
Yeah.

361
00:18:57,203 --> 00:18:59,336
Do you have a minute?

362
00:18:59,405 --> 00:19:01,338
Sure.

363
00:19:06,146 --> 00:19:07,378
Tape's still in the machine,

364
00:19:07,447 --> 00:19:09,313
so we'll plug it in
and it should come up.

365
00:19:09,382 --> 00:19:10,559
And what we'll see is whatever

366
00:19:10,583 --> 00:19:12,328
Dan Galloway saw
when he unplugged it?

367
00:19:12,352 --> 00:19:14,285
That's right.

368
00:19:20,627 --> 00:19:22,560
Well, I'll be damned.

369
00:19:25,165 --> 00:19:27,865
Yes, I stormed off
the set and, yes,

370
00:19:27,934 --> 00:19:30,401
I was murderously
angry at Dan Galloway.

371
00:19:30,469 --> 00:19:31,802
You can understand why.

372
00:19:31,871 --> 00:19:34,705
Oh, oh, sure, sure.
Man was a jerk.

373
00:19:34,774 --> 00:19:36,407
Yes.

374
00:19:36,476 --> 00:19:38,942
But I did not kill him.

375
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:41,779
Now, I would like to discuss
this with you at length,

376
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,414
but I'm preparing a decision

377
00:19:43,483 --> 00:19:44,893
that I have to
render this afternoon,

378
00:19:44,917 --> 00:19:46,951
so I must ask you to excuse me.

379
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:50,288
It's lunchtime, so
why couldn't we...

380
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:51,956
I'm lunching in.

381
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:54,625
Perhaps we can talk
tomorrow. Call me.

382
00:19:54,694 --> 00:19:56,960
Judge Cordante, would you say

383
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,530
that Dan Galloway
was the kind of person

384
00:19:59,599 --> 00:20:02,533
who ever did anything
without a purpose?

385
00:20:02,602 --> 00:20:04,969
Mr. Matlock,

386
00:20:05,038 --> 00:20:06,181
I really am busy.

387
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,872
A-A-At the moment he was killed,

388
00:20:08,941 --> 00:20:12,476
he was watching a tape of
the show that you appeared on.

389
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:14,611
Yes. Although he was dying,

390
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:17,248
he left, what I believe,
was a dying message.

391
00:20:17,317 --> 00:20:21,185
He pulled the plug
from an editing machine

392
00:20:21,253 --> 00:20:24,755
so the tape would
end on your face.

393
00:20:24,824 --> 00:20:27,525
Me? Yes, your face

394
00:20:27,594 --> 00:20:30,428
was on the screen
when Dan Galloway died.

395
00:20:33,533 --> 00:20:35,866
Mr. Matlock, if this is

396
00:20:35,935 --> 00:20:37,779
how you plan to build
a case against me,

397
00:20:37,803 --> 00:20:40,237
I would suggest that you
look for another profession.

398
00:20:40,305 --> 00:20:42,406
Now, really, I must
get back to work.

399
00:20:42,475 --> 00:20:45,242
I'm not building anything, yet.

400
00:20:45,311 --> 00:20:48,045
It would just seem to me,
that, as an officer of the court,

401
00:20:48,114 --> 00:20:50,214
you'd be more cooperative.

402
00:20:52,051 --> 00:20:54,218
All right.

403
00:20:54,287 --> 00:20:57,487
Now, it's my understanding
that the murder happened

404
00:20:57,556 --> 00:20:59,556
between 7:00 and 7:15.

405
00:20:59,625 --> 00:21:01,469
And I know for a
fact that by then,

406
00:21:01,493 --> 00:21:03,573
I was already having
dinner with a friend.

407
00:21:04,663 --> 00:21:06,363
Now, I must insist that you go.

408
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,672
If you have any more questions,

409
00:21:07,734 --> 00:21:09,666
call me in the morning. Okay.

410
00:21:09,736 --> 00:21:12,069
But, uh, why,

411
00:21:12,138 --> 00:21:14,404
why would a woman
of your stature,

412
00:21:14,473 --> 00:21:18,475
a judge, agree to appear
on the<i> Galloway</i> show?

413
00:21:20,679 --> 00:21:23,447
Well, um...

414
00:21:23,515 --> 00:21:25,116
Well, I wanted to host

415
00:21:25,184 --> 00:21:27,985
his new legal advice
show,<i> Real Law.</i>

416
00:21:28,054 --> 00:21:30,454
<i>Real Law.</i>

417
00:21:30,522 --> 00:21:33,724
No, I'm not going to give
up law for show business,

418
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:36,526
at least not permanently,
but, well, I did think

419
00:21:36,595 --> 00:21:38,974
it would be interesting
and lucrative for awhile.

420
00:21:38,998 --> 00:21:41,610
Yeah. Well, it hasn't
hurt Judge Wapner.

421
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:43,567
No, I guess not.

422
00:21:46,538 --> 00:21:49,140
Of course, he actually
<i>is</i> in show business.

423
00:21:53,212 --> 00:21:54,456
I should have called you, Phil.

424
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,191
Her Honor's lunching out today.

425
00:21:56,215 --> 00:21:58,149
Don't worry, I'll pay you.

426
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:04,421
♪ ♪

427
00:22:21,074 --> 00:22:23,006
♪ ♪

428
00:22:39,192 --> 00:22:42,126
Mr. Matlock, what
are you doing here?

429
00:22:42,195 --> 00:22:45,829
I thought we'd finish our
conversation over lunch.

430
00:22:45,898 --> 00:22:48,365
You're David Cabot.

431
00:22:48,434 --> 00:22:50,067
That's right.

432
00:22:50,136 --> 00:22:51,968
Your Honor,

433
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:54,048
you shouldn't be
seen with this man.

434
00:22:54,072 --> 00:22:55,705
That's none of your business.

435
00:22:55,774 --> 00:22:57,885
But he's all over the papers,

436
00:22:57,909 --> 00:23:00,469
indicted for tax fraud,
SEC violations...

437
00:23:00,513 --> 00:23:03,313
Indicted, not convicted.

438
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:05,883
And Judge Cordante
is free to be seen

439
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:07,217
with whomever she likes.

440
00:23:07,286 --> 00:23:09,452
She can't feel that free.

441
00:23:09,521 --> 00:23:11,299
Otherwise, she'd see
you out in the open,

442
00:23:11,323 --> 00:23:13,402
not hiding under some fishpond.

443
00:23:13,426 --> 00:23:16,359
I don't like what you're
insinuating, Mr. Matlock.

444
00:23:16,429 --> 00:23:18,273
I'll say it right out loud.

445
00:23:18,297 --> 00:23:19,808
Being seen with you could hurt

446
00:23:19,832 --> 00:23:23,600
the judge's
reputation and career.

447
00:23:23,669 --> 00:23:27,070
Mr. Matlock, I will answer
your questions right now.

448
00:23:27,139 --> 00:23:29,050
You know what I want to know.

449
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:31,220
Who were you with at
the time of the murder?

450
00:23:31,244 --> 00:23:32,910
She was with me.

451
00:23:32,979 --> 00:23:35,111
You'll testify to that?

452
00:23:35,181 --> 00:23:36,613
Of course.

453
00:23:36,682 --> 00:23:38,615
Is that what you want?

454
00:23:38,684 --> 00:23:40,950
No!

455
00:23:41,019 --> 00:23:44,788
I mean, I was with David, but...

456
00:23:44,856 --> 00:23:46,790
Please.

457
00:23:51,029 --> 00:23:53,441
Your Honor, you're placing me

458
00:23:53,465 --> 00:23:56,534
in a very awkward position.

459
00:23:58,638 --> 00:24:00,816
I'll tell you what I'll do.

460
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:03,151
I'll keep this little
bit of information

461
00:24:03,175 --> 00:24:06,109
in my hip pocket for a while.

462
00:24:06,178 --> 00:24:07,777
Good luck to you.

463
00:24:07,847 --> 00:24:09,612
Thank you.

464
00:24:09,681 --> 00:24:11,448
I can't wish you luck.

465
00:24:13,553 --> 00:24:16,220
I've read the charges
against you, and

466
00:24:16,289 --> 00:24:19,889
I'll just wish you a miracle.

467
00:24:31,770 --> 00:24:33,036
You saw Judge Cordante?

468
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:34,437
Yeah.

469
00:24:34,507 --> 00:24:36,439
Maybe she's sowing
a few wild oats,

470
00:24:36,509 --> 00:24:38,775
or getting a little
poison out of her system.

471
00:24:38,844 --> 00:24:40,489
What are you talking about?

472
00:24:40,513 --> 00:24:43,780
Well, pretty soon she may
be in another line of work.

473
00:24:43,849 --> 00:24:45,827
But she does have an alibi.

474
00:24:45,851 --> 00:24:48,329
But Dan Galloway
went to a lot of trouble

475
00:24:48,353 --> 00:24:50,331
to name her as the
killer before he died.

476
00:24:50,355 --> 00:24:52,990
Well, maybe he's trying
to tell us something else.

477
00:24:53,058 --> 00:24:54,135
What?

478
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:56,472
We have nothing to go on.

479
00:24:56,496 --> 00:24:58,428
No.

480
00:24:58,498 --> 00:25:00,564
Not much.

481
00:25:10,709 --> 00:25:12,676
<i>I don't understand it.</i>

482
00:25:12,745 --> 00:25:14,845
Well, you knew him.

483
00:25:14,913 --> 00:25:16,847
That was the style.

484
00:25:16,915 --> 00:25:19,850
I'm sorry it worked
out this way.

485
00:25:19,918 --> 00:25:22,853
Well, it's not your fault.

486
00:25:22,921 --> 00:25:24,899
So, what happens to you now?

487
00:25:24,923 --> 00:25:26,056
Well, with Dan dead,

488
00:25:26,125 --> 00:25:28,058
the corporation's
asked me to stay on.

489
00:25:28,127 --> 00:25:30,060
Oh. Oh, hello.

490
00:25:30,129 --> 00:25:32,062
Oh, you're Miss Wilson.

491
00:25:32,131 --> 00:25:34,109
Yes. Uh, Ben Matlock.

492
00:25:34,133 --> 00:25:36,111
Oh, yes, you're
Lisa's attorney, right?

493
00:25:36,135 --> 00:25:37,613
Yeah. Yeah.

494
00:25:37,637 --> 00:25:41,238
I understand that you used
to work with, uh, Dan Galloway

495
00:25:41,307 --> 00:25:43,707
and didn't, uh... You
didn't part as friends.

496
00:25:43,776 --> 00:25:46,710
Well, Mr. Matlock,
that was five years ago.

497
00:25:46,779 --> 00:25:48,423
Ancient history. Yeah.

498
00:25:48,447 --> 00:25:51,081
But then he invited you
down here to do his show,

499
00:25:51,150 --> 00:25:53,116
and humiliated you.

500
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:56,119
You'd think I'd know
better, wouldn't you?

501
00:25:56,188 --> 00:25:59,022
Well, I'd be the first to admit
that Dan Galloway was a...

502
00:25:59,091 --> 00:26:00,802
A jerk, yeah.

503
00:26:00,826 --> 00:26:02,136
But I didn't kill him. Yeah.

504
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:05,929
Uh, what did you do, uh,
after the taping was finished?

505
00:26:05,997 --> 00:26:08,599
All I really wanted
to do was get home.

506
00:26:08,668 --> 00:26:10,267
So, I ran back to my motel.

507
00:26:10,335 --> 00:26:13,703
I packed, checked out and
drove back to Bakersfield.

508
00:26:13,773 --> 00:26:15,739
I see.

509
00:26:15,808 --> 00:26:17,586
Thanks again, Lisa.
You've been great.

510
00:26:17,610 --> 00:26:21,010
And good luck to you,
Mr. Matlock. Thank you.

511
00:26:21,614 --> 00:26:23,046
What'd she want?

512
00:26:23,115 --> 00:26:24,593
She wanted to know
about the possibility

513
00:26:24,617 --> 00:26:26,550
of hosting<i> Real Law.</i>

514
00:26:26,619 --> 00:26:27,818
Dan promised it to her.

515
00:26:27,886 --> 00:26:29,166
It was gonna be
her big comeback.

516
00:26:29,221 --> 00:26:32,155
His way of making
up for the past.

517
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:33,468
Well, that's interesting.

518
00:26:33,492 --> 00:26:36,427
He promised the
same job to Marla.

519
00:26:36,495 --> 00:26:37,928
What's even more interesting is

520
00:26:37,996 --> 00:26:40,096
I set the host for the
show a month ago,

521
00:26:40,165 --> 00:26:42,098
and Dan knew it.

522
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:44,567
Huh.

523
00:26:49,175 --> 00:26:51,107
Three women who...
You know what I think?

524
00:26:51,177 --> 00:26:52,354
All personal friends of mine...

525
00:26:52,378 --> 00:26:55,312
I think that button's
got nothing to do with it.

526
00:26:55,381 --> 00:26:56,591
Wait, wait.

527
