and ran right down here.

789
00:38:18,964 --> 00:38:20,063
Why?

790
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:21,731
What did he say to you?

791
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:25,067
He told me I'd be the perfect
guest on a show he was planning.

792
00:38:25,137 --> 00:38:29,772
After five years of silence
and all he did to you?

793
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:37,847
Isn't it true that you
agreed to be on his show

794
00:38:37,915 --> 00:38:43,019
because he promised to
give you the position of host

795
00:38:43,088 --> 00:38:46,556
on a new talk show?

796
00:38:46,624 --> 00:38:48,157
He did mention that.

797
00:38:48,226 --> 00:38:52,128
Did he also mention
that the position of host

798
00:38:52,197 --> 00:38:53,930
had already been set

799
00:38:53,999 --> 00:38:58,201
and that it had been offered
to several other women?

800
00:39:00,071 --> 00:39:01,170
No.

801
00:39:01,239 --> 00:39:02,338
Yeah.

802
00:39:02,406 --> 00:39:06,075
I have a signed
affidavit right here

803
00:39:06,144 --> 00:39:10,613
from Judge Marla Cordante...

804
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:13,182
which says that

805
00:39:13,251 --> 00:39:18,821
he offered her
that same position.

806
00:39:18,890 --> 00:39:20,689
Dan Galloway

807
00:39:20,759 --> 00:39:22,158
was a terrible man.

808
00:39:22,227 --> 00:39:24,460
He was a world-class jerk.

809
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:28,431
He liked to play games
with people's lives.

810
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:30,867
Any number would've
wanted him dead,

811
00:39:30,935 --> 00:39:32,869
but only one
could've killed him.

812
00:39:32,937 --> 00:39:36,105
And unfortunately
for him or her,

813
00:39:36,173 --> 00:39:41,644
he played one last
game just before he died.

814
00:39:41,713 --> 00:39:45,348
He left a clue.

815
00:39:45,417 --> 00:39:47,082
Bailiff?

816
00:39:52,657 --> 00:39:55,958
When Judge Cordante's
picture appeared on the monitor

817
00:39:56,027 --> 00:39:57,960
we thought he
was trying to tell us

818
00:39:58,029 --> 00:39:59,895
that she had killed him

819
00:39:59,964 --> 00:40:02,865
but then we have to
remember he was dying.

820
00:40:02,933 --> 00:40:05,034
He was on the floor.

821
00:40:05,102 --> 00:40:08,737
He was looking at the
monitor upside down.

822
00:40:08,806 --> 00:40:11,073
And when he pulled that plug,

823
00:40:11,142 --> 00:40:18,881
this digital counter
stopped at 337.

824
00:40:18,950 --> 00:40:21,484
But if you look
at it upside down,

825
00:40:21,553 --> 00:40:24,286
the way he did,

826
00:40:24,355 --> 00:40:27,356
it spells "L-E-E."

827
00:40:28,894 --> 00:40:30,459
You see that, Leanne?

828
00:40:30,529 --> 00:40:34,897
As you said, Dan was a jerk.

829
00:40:34,966 --> 00:40:38,534
All this means is that he
was trying to set me up again.

830
00:40:38,603 --> 00:40:41,070
And besides, at the
time he was killed,

831
00:40:41,139 --> 00:40:42,817
I was already
back in Bakersfield.

832
00:40:42,841 --> 00:40:43,940
No.

833
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:46,542
Thank you.

834
00:40:47,678 --> 00:40:50,946
You checked out
of the motel at 6:00.

835
00:40:54,286 --> 00:40:57,853
But you left your car
in the motel garage

836
00:40:57,922 --> 00:40:59,855
until almost 8:00.

837
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:02,892
That places you in Los Angeles

838
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,472
well within the
time of the murder.

839
00:41:04,496 --> 00:41:07,530
As a matter of fact, it places
you at the scene of the crime,

840
00:41:07,599 --> 00:41:09,999
and before you
say I have no proof,

841
00:41:10,068 --> 00:41:13,636
I'm gonna take a shot at it.

842
00:41:13,705 --> 00:41:19,709
This button was found on
the floor of the editing room

843
00:41:19,777 --> 00:41:21,110
where Dan Galloway was killed.

844
00:41:21,179 --> 00:41:23,079
I guess the police
thought it wasn't important

845
00:41:23,148 --> 00:41:25,347
and I didn't at first.

846
00:41:25,416 --> 00:41:30,285
But you know, they
vacuum that room every night

847
00:41:30,355 --> 00:41:32,200
and just four days
before the murder,

848
00:41:32,224 --> 00:41:34,023
that room was recarpeted.

849
00:41:34,092 --> 00:41:39,028
The old carpet was thrown away.

850
00:41:39,097 --> 00:41:41,731
Somebody who owns this button

851
00:41:41,799 --> 00:41:44,968
has to be involved
in this whole thing.

852
00:41:45,036 --> 00:41:47,270
Somebody. Objection!

853
00:41:47,339 --> 00:41:50,072
Your Honor, I don't know
how they try cases in Atlanta,

854
00:41:50,141 --> 00:41:52,508
but this is the time for
questioning the witness,

855
00:41:52,577 --> 00:41:54,655
not for argument,
so... Your Honor,

856
00:41:54,679 --> 00:41:58,381
four days before the murder,
the room was recarpeted.

857
00:41:58,449 --> 00:42:00,616
The old carpeting and
everything that was on it

858
00:42:00,685 --> 00:42:02,251
was torn up and thrown away.

859
00:42:02,320 --> 00:42:03,886
This button is evidence.

860
00:42:03,955 --> 00:42:05,521
Objection overruled.

861
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:06,667
Continue, Mr. Matlock.

862
00:42:06,691 --> 00:42:08,757
Thank you.

863
00:42:08,826 --> 00:42:12,728
But it doesn't seem
to belong to anybody.

864
00:42:12,797 --> 00:42:15,898
It doesn't seem to
come off anything.

865
00:42:15,966 --> 00:42:18,801
It doesn't seem to
have done anything.

866
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:23,906
When you came down,
uh, to do the taping,

867
00:42:23,975 --> 00:42:26,642
you were wearing a jacket
but then when you actually

868
00:42:26,711 --> 00:42:29,311
did the taping, you
weren't wearing the jacket.

869
00:42:29,381 --> 00:42:30,847
Some sort of sound problem.

870
00:42:30,916 --> 00:42:33,316
I wore my red jacket.

871
00:42:33,385 --> 00:42:35,129
It doesn't have
any brass buttons,

872
00:42:35,153 --> 00:42:36,619
Mr. Matlock.

873
00:42:36,688 --> 00:42:39,088
Not on the outside.

874
00:42:39,157 --> 00:42:42,659
But all double-breasted coats

875
00:42:42,727 --> 00:42:44,961
have buttons on the inside

876
00:42:45,030 --> 00:42:46,962
to make sure they hang right.

877
00:42:47,032 --> 00:42:51,234
Now, your jacket was made by...

878
00:42:53,671 --> 00:42:56,205
Francesca di Giovanni?

879
00:42:56,274 --> 00:42:58,141
Right? Yes.

880
00:42:58,209 --> 00:42:59,209
Bailiff?

881
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:08,551
Now, this is a rack of
Miss Giovanni's jackets.

882
00:43:08,620 --> 00:43:12,187
And as you can see,

883
00:43:12,257 --> 00:43:17,092
the inside buttons are brass.

884
00:43:18,929 --> 00:43:20,829
See?

885
00:43:20,898 --> 00:43:24,500
Brass.

886
00:43:24,569 --> 00:43:27,303
All brass.

887
00:43:27,372 --> 00:43:31,106
Just like this button that
was found on the floor

888
00:43:31,175 --> 00:43:35,411
by Dan Galloway's body.

889
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:40,015
Now, you recognize
this jacket, don't you?

890
00:43:40,085 --> 00:43:42,985
It's yours, isn't it?

891
00:43:43,054 --> 00:43:47,757
I remember spilling coffee
on the sleeve the other day.

892
00:43:47,825 --> 00:43:53,295
But your inside button doesn't
match the brass buttons.

893
00:43:53,365 --> 00:43:55,464
Your inside button
is white, isn't it?

894
00:43:55,533 --> 00:43:59,435
I lost the original
button months ago.

895
00:43:59,504 --> 00:44:00,669
I don't think so.

896
00:44:00,738 --> 00:44:03,539
I think you lost this button

897
00:44:03,608 --> 00:44:07,276
when you raised the
axe to kill Dan Galloway.

898
00:44:07,345 --> 00:44:09,145
No.

899
00:44:09,214 --> 00:44:12,614
I distinctly remember I
lost the button last October.

900
00:44:12,683 --> 00:44:15,718
At a country club wedding
reception that I planned.

901
00:44:15,787 --> 00:44:17,519
Then why did you wait

902
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:20,522
till the day after Dan
Galloway was killed

903
00:44:20,591 --> 00:44:21,891
to take your coat

904
00:44:21,959 --> 00:44:25,460
to the Forest
Drycleaners in Bakersfield

905
00:44:25,529 --> 00:44:28,998
and have them
replace this button?

906
00:44:29,067 --> 00:44:32,801
The cleaner's mark
is still inside the jacket.

907
00:44:32,870 --> 00:44:34,570
And we talked to the management.

908
00:44:36,908 --> 00:44:41,243
Why did you wait

909
00:44:41,312 --> 00:44:44,580
till the day after Dan
Galloway was killed

910
00:44:44,649 --> 00:44:46,949
to replace this button?

911
00:44:49,454 --> 00:44:51,487
Can you answer that?

912
00:44:59,897 --> 00:45:03,699
Would you like to
retain an attorney?

913
00:45:07,405 --> 00:45:09,005
Yes.

914
00:45:09,074 --> 00:45:11,674
That's wise.

915
00:45:16,114 --> 00:45:17,780
No further questions.

916
00:45:23,755 --> 00:45:27,456
We find the defendant,
Lisa Bateman, not guilty.

917
00:45:27,525 --> 00:45:29,424
Court is adjourned.

918
00:45:31,028 --> 00:45:32,628
Thank you!

919
00:45:32,697 --> 00:45:34,663
And how you did
it, I don't know.

920
00:45:34,732 --> 00:45:36,198
Well, it wasn't easy.

921
00:45:36,266 --> 00:45:37,432
Can I take you to dinner?

922
00:45:37,502 --> 00:45:41,203
Oh, well, thanks
but I guess I'm,

923
00:45:41,271 --> 00:45:43,639
I guess I'm pretty
much a home boy.

924
00:45:43,708 --> 00:45:46,274
A home boy?

925
00:45:46,344 --> 00:45:49,846
Yeah, yeah, I'm gonna go
home, Atlanta, get a bite to eat,

926
00:45:49,914 --> 00:45:53,282
maybe a hot dog all the way,

927
00:45:53,351 --> 00:45:55,818
put on my green striped
pajamas, go to bed.

928
00:45:55,887 --> 00:45:57,686
Okay.

929
00:45:57,755 --> 00:45:59,188
How about you?

930
00:45:59,257 --> 00:46:02,958
Well, aside from the hot dog
and the green striped pajamas,

931
00:46:03,027 --> 00:46:06,195
I guess I'm pretty
much a home girl.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
